From fd4c4267a20496883dca329d824911e1f9d412c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:11:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Test and document the non linear solver of KINSOL

KINSOLSolverTest (sequential, parallel, and on a GPU when the tests on
the GPU are enabled) compares each strategy of KINSOL with the Newton
solver on the uniaxial tension of a plastic cube: Newton's method with
and without line search (8 iterations, as the Newton solver), the
tangent operator updated every three iterations (14), Picard's method
(59), with Anderson's acceleration (32), damped (70) or with updates of
the tangent operator (17), a stagnation below the floor of the rounding
errors (accepted), a failure of the linear solver (stopped at the first
iteration), and the refusals of invalid options.
